to-studio 007 (C2 Games, 2026-11-10, branch claude/r8-play-seam): the phone play piece's because never reaches the reply.

Found by tests/r8-play-phone-seam.test.mjs (Studio's phone door → buildLive → /api/play/level → /act → the lesson turn, four
pilot topics × seeded learners at p360).

What is wrong (server/studio/seam.js phonePlayFor):
1. The piece's facts get a top-level `because` string ("phone: <family> covers this skill"). The facts row the reply reads is
   factsRowForSlot → rowOf, and rowOf prints only `archetype` and `onScreen`: the string never reaches the teacher, though the
   docstring says it goes "into the facts row".
2. buildLive returns `r.because`: the picker's own records (e.g. kind play.pick_mixup "open mix-up: Confuses perimeter with
   area ..., 0.82" for a seeded learner, play.pick_fit, play.fade_history) and the play side's studio_gate record. Studio
   drops them: the comment "theirs wins where both are present" is not implemented. The records do ride the signed session
   (/api/play/level and the seam row's `chose=` at level end), so the lesson only learns WHY this game after it ends.

The change: keep `piece.because` (the stagecraft test matches it), add `piece.becauseRecords` (the play side's records), and
put the lead record's kind (the first non-gate record, else studio_gate) into onScreen as `chose`, right after `game`, so the
row reads e.g. "… play@1 · game nazariya/floor · chose pick_mixup · …" (values only, no prose, inside ROW_MAX). No child
why-line: `chose` is a kind word, and the play side never makes a line from studio_gate (server/play/why.js WHY_REASON).
`git apply --check` passes on claude/r8-play-seam (b3b076a18 + this branch). Not applied by C2 (Studio's file).

